; D8-v2 shape-only surface validation: a sugar form whose `:ref`
; points at a target elsewhere in the document.
;
; Surface validation in `lowerOneForm` builds a one-form sub-tree
; containing only `(sugar :ref t0)`. Its cross-ref index sees only
; that form, so the `:ref` lookup misses with `not_cross_ref`. With
; v1 `surface.hasErrors()` fires and the hook is silently skipped —
; the source `(sugar …)` then validates against its sugar schema and
; the fixture's diagnostic stream depends on whether the cross-ref
; against `(target :name t0)` resolves *in the source tree*. With v2
; (commit 3) the cross-ref miss is filtered from the gate decision,
; the hook runs, `(sugar-normal :ref t0)` lands in the lowered tree,
; and the forest pass resolves the ref against the source target.
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name target-ref :underlying symbol
    :cross-ref (cross-ref :target target))
  (form :name target
    (key :name name :type symbol :optional false))
  (form :name sugar
    (key :name ref :type target-ref :optional false)
    :lowering (lowering :hook test/identity-v1 :produces [sugar-normal]))
  (form :name sugar-normal
    (key :name ref :type target-ref :optional false)))

(target :name t0)
(sugar :ref t0)
